 "type": "FeatureCollection",
 "description": "Late patches (applied after the sea mesh is built): harbours whose water areas the sea graph does not reach: each link is a straight line over open water (checked against the OSM land polygons) from the harbour's own water network to the nearest node of the sea graph. Vila Real de Santo António: the Guadiana mouth (159 m). Saltsjöbaden: Baggensfjärden to Ingaröfjärden (1.3 km). Göteborg: the Göta älv mouth below the Älvsborg bridge (340 m). Longer links follow the shortest water path on an 8-10 m land raster (OSM land polygons), from sea-graph node to sea-graph node: Baggensstäket, Lännerstasundet and Skurusundet (8.6 km; the strait is 15-30 m wide, narrower than the finest sea mesh), Älvsborgsfjorden to Öckerö past Hönö (11.7 km; the coarse mesh sent Göteborg -> Öckerö 33 km round the outside), and Fethiye bay to the town harbour (8.4 km; the harbour's own small mesh was not joined to the gulf).",
